## Goal
Reject UI::Selectable(label, selected, flags, size) — Openplanet only exposes the 3-arg form.

## Source
todo-cover-cases-next.txt — Case 4 (2026-04-20, tm-agent)

## Repro
```angelscript
if (UI::Selectable(hitLabel, msg.expanded, 0, vec2(availW, rowH))) { ... }
```

## Compiler (game-side)
```
ChatUI.as (826, 13) : error: No matching signatures to
    'UI::Selectable(string, bool&, const int, vec2)'
Candidates are:
    bool UI::Selectable(const string&in label, bool selected,
                        int flags = UI::SelectableFlags::None)
```

## Workaround
Use `UI::InvisibleButton(id, vec2)` for custom-drawn clickable rows.
ImGui upstream has Selectable(..., size); Openplanet bindings do not.

## Acceptance
- [ ] 4-arg UI::Selectable diagnosed
- [ ] Valid 2- and 3-arg forms silent
- [ ] Regression test

## Notes
Same systemic gap as IndexOf: member/namespace calls skip arity checks. Prefer shared external arity path over one-off Selectable handling.

Fixed by B003 external arity work. Regression tests on master: external_ui_selectable_four_arg_fires, external_ui_selectable_valid_arity_ok.